  "malware_family": "OXLOADER (loader) delivering CASTLESTEALER",
  "threat_actor": "Unnamed Russian-speaking, financially motivated actor (CIS/Russian exclusions; Google Ads advertiser ВОЛОДИМИР ТЕРЕЩЕНКО)",
  "platforms": [
    "windows"
  ],
  "summary": "OXLOADER is a previously undocumented Windows loader delivered through malicious Google Ads impersonating Node.js; it abuses the PE .reloc section and a new RWX .xtext section in a renamed copy of dui70.dll to stage shellcode, then bootstraps CASTLESTEALER in memory via Donut shellcode. It layers control-flow flattening, MBA/opaque predicates, self-modifying rolling-XOR decryption stubs and Adler-32 API hashing, plus anti-VM checks (WNetAddConnection2W emulation, CPU/RAM/refresh-rate thresholds) and CIS/Russian-language exclusions. Detection can key on the .reloc-resident shellcode bytes, the AFX_WM_DRAW2D clipboard-format call from the hijacked CRT initializer, the obf_xor_a1_with_a2_plus_33FDA routine and the CASTLESTEALER AES config key.",
